198
01:01:42,560 --> 01:01:56,260
AMLC Executive Director Atty. Ronel U. Buenaventura: So, Your Honor, AMLC po is created pursuant to the Anti-Money Laundering Act or RA 916. Ito po yung Philippine Financial Intelligence Unit po.

199
01:01:56,500 --> 01:01:58,820
Atty. Mae Sancho Divinagracia: Ano naman po ang mandato ng AMLC?

200
01:01:59,820 --> 01:02:09,220
AMLC Executive Director Atty. Ronel U. Buenaventura: Ang mandato po is to ensure po that the Philippines will not be used as a money laundering site for the proceeds of unlawful activity po, Your Honor.

201
01:02:09,580 --> 01:02:12,900
Atty. Mae Sancho Divinagracia: At ano naman po ang mga kapangyarihan at tungkulin ng AMLC?

202
01:02:13,530 --> 01:03:10,720
AMLC Executive Director Atty. Ronel U. Buenaventura: So kasama po sa tungkulin po ng AMLC ay to require and receive covered transaction reports or CTRs and suspicious transaction reports po or STRs. and then i-analyze po ito and if needed to conduct necessary investigation including filing of bank inquiry or freeze order po before the court of appeals and then if proper if all evidence po ay meron to file the necessary criminal case before the criminal complaint before the office of the ombudsman or the department of justice and to file for future cases of proceeds of money laundering. Part din po ng mandato ng AMLC yung mag-supervise po ng mga covered person to ensure that they comply with the Anti-Money Laundering Act.

203
01:03:11,240 --> 01:03:19,180
Atty. Mae Sancho Divinagracia: Atty. Benaventura, paulit-ulit din po nabanggit ang salitang money laundering. In simple terms, Atty. Benaventura, ano po ba ang money laundering?

204
01:03:21,400 --> 01:04:01,720
AMLC Executive Director Atty. Ronel U. Buenaventura: Your Honor, I'll be recalling from the law and jurisprudence that I remember right now. Money laundering is a crime whereby proceeds from unlawful activity listed under the law are transferred, transacted, moved, or made to appear to have originated from legitimate sources. So, essentially po, ito po yung pagtatago or pagpapalabas na yung pera galing sa illegal activity ay malinis po.

205
01:04:02,040 --> 01:04:11,440
Atty. Mae Sancho Divinagracia: Okay. Kanina rin po nabanggit ninyo na tumatanggap ang AMLC ng mga covered at suspicious transaction reports. Saan po ba galing ang mga reports na ito?

206
01:04:11,820 --> 01:04:19,400
AMLC Executive Director Atty. Ronel U. Buenaventura: Yung cover, galing po sila sa covered persons po, Your Honor. Sila po yung nagpa-file sa amin.

207
01:04:19,710 --> 01:04:22,410
Atty. Mae Sancho Divinagracia: Sino naman po itong mga tinatawag na covered persons?

208
01:04:23,830 --> 01:05:31,460
AMLC Executive Director Atty. Ronel U. Buenaventura: Covered persons po, ayon po sa batas, meron pong apat na grupo po. Yung unang grupo po, ito po yung mga supervised and regulated po ni Bangko Sentral ng Pilipinas. So kasama po dito yung mga banko, remittance company, e-wallet, at iba pa. Yung pangalawa naman po ay mga regulated po ng insurance commission. Kasama po rito yung mga insurance company, pre-need companies, at iba pa po. Yung pangatlo naman po, yung regulated po ng Securities and Exchange Commission kasama po dito yung mga securities broker, securities dealer, investment houses, at iba pa. At yung huling grupo naman po, hindi po sila regulated yung tatlong nabanggit ko pong ahensya pero Nakalagay po sila sa batas. So ang tawag po namin sa kanila ay designated non-financial businesses and professions or DNFBPs. Sila naman po kasama po dito yung mga casinos, jewelry dealers, real estate broker, real estate developers at iba pa po. So sila po yung mga covered persons po natin.

209
01:05:31,460 --> 01:05:36,420
Atty. Mae Sancho Divinagracia: Punta muna po tayo sa covered transaction report. Ano naman po itong mga covered transactions na ito?

210
01:05:36,870 --> 01:06:07,650
AMLC Executive Director Atty. Ronel U. Buenaventura: Your Honor, yung covered transaction is any transaction in cash or monetary instrument in excess of 500,000 pesos in a banking day. Kung ang reporting entity po ay casino, ang halaga po ay 5 million pesos in cash. At kung ang reporting, ang covered person na nagre-report naman po ay Royal estate broker or developer that is 7.5 million in cash po.

